<title>FINLAND: Outokumpu says overcapacity clouds metals.</title>
<headline>Outokumpu says overcapacity clouds metals.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish metals and mining group Outokumpu Oy said in a statement on Monday overcapacity in copper and stainless steel was clouding the outlook for metals markets in the near term.</p>
<p>&quot;The outlook in the metals markets for the near future is overshadowed by global overcapacity in both copper and stainless steel production,&quot; it said in a statement with its 1996 results.</p>
<p>In Europe, it said copper inventories were very low at the end of last year and stainless steel stocks had returned to almost normal levels, but inventories of zinc and nickel were still &quot;very high&quot;.</p>
</text>
